Z||000000||pHoOl||10-30-2001||01:40 PM||||Don't start drooling, i'm talking 0-60, not quarter mile.  Okay... so since the last time i posted about this, i fixed the TPS (it was sticking at wide open throttle) and put in a K&N.  <P>Anybody have ideas on what's wrong?  I was thinking that the cat might be clogged since to my knowledge it hasnt' been changed since new.  but someone from the forum told me that the exhaust manifold would be glowing red hot if this were the case, which it does not seem to be.  The car has 130K miles on it, so it doesn't seem like it should be crapping out yet.<P>Anyone have ideas on how i can check for a clogged cat, or any other things that might be slowing me way down?  I'm thinking in spring that i'll cut the cat off and find out if that helps, and maybe tear apart the intake system to see if there is a major hairball or something in it.  <P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
