Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-30-2001||02:20 PM||||theres a couple differnt ways to test for a bad cat... 1) exhaust pressure guage, or 2) take it off and replace it. do you have emissions testing where you are? if not just ditch it. if so I've got a Hi-flow unit brand new $125 shipped. it's a 2.25" unit i've got 2.5" you can do the math. do you manifolds glow red/orange? does it start fine but not rev worth a crap?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||10-30-2001||02:35 PM||||To check your cat, either borrow one of those laser thermometers and check tem before and after the cat.  Or you can just feel(or see now that its cold out) how much exhuast is coming out.  If it isn't much...you've got a problem.<P>The only good cat is a hollow one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||10-30-2001||02:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B><BR>The only good cat is a hollow one.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I like that one. <BR>Here in CA emissions is a big deal. You wouldn't want us to make so much smog that it drifts up to where you are do you?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I don't know about the catalytic converter but one thing I know for sure is that your car will 'look' much faster with the wing. Mine sure did!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FormulaJoe||10-30-2001||04:15 PM||||One of the things I noticed when I was driving my Formula with a plugged cat was how loud the intake was.  I am talking with the window down I could hear the air being pulled into the intake on the side of the car.  Made a kind of roaring noise, and the car had no power  past about 3000 rpm..  When I pulled the cat  and looked through it there was a small place up in one of the corners about the size of a silver dollar (the old big ones) that you could see light through.  The rest of the honeycomb of the converter was melted closed.  Now I can hear the exhaust and don't hear the intake.||||reg||1
Z||000007||pHoOl||10-30-2001||04:41 PM||||I do hear a bit of intake.  Also, it doesn't seem like much exhaust comes out the pipes. I haven't noticed the manifold glowing, i looked at it at night after driving a bit.  But at the same time, i don't exactly know where the exhaust manifold is.  (not that car literate)   <P>As for how much exhaust is coming out... there is a lil bit, not like a constant stream out of the pipes.  Kinda looks like when someone smokes and just lets if gently roll out instead of exhaling.  (sorry, best way i could think to describe it)  I"m gonna go take out in a lil bit, and see what else i can learn.<P>As for removing the Cat... Is this something that i can do in the parking lot at college provided the owner of the car says it's okay?  or should i just wait til spring?<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
