Z||000020||Smoooooth GT||10-31-2001||12:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kasdan:<BR><B>I noticed my manifolds the day my drivers side tires decided to dry-rot to hell....does this mean i have a clogged cat?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have also heard that If you have a vacuumm leak that they will also glo red at night.. OR was I just hearing thing's..?? Steve<P>------------------<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Jefrysuko||10-31-2001||09:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B> I have also heard that If you have a vacuumm leak that they will also glo red at night.. OR was I just hearing thing's..?? Steve<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No you are right.  I have witnessed the manifolds glowing due to a vacuum leak.  I havn't ever seen this from a plugged cat.  The reason they glow when you have a vacuum leak is because your engine is running extreamly lean.  This makes for increased exhaust temperatures expecially at the exhaust ports.  With a plugged cat your engine will be running rich if anything which causes lower exhaust temperatures.  Granted the exhaust is being trapped and at a higher pressure but this shouldn't affect the temperature all that much.  I would imagine that 1st2m6 was confusing the symptoms.  I might be wrong though, anyone actually experience glowing manifolds with only a plugged cat and no vacuum leak?||||reg||1
Z||000022||87GTZ34||10-31-2001||10:46 AM||||Your exhaust doesn't have to glow to have a clogged cat.  It depends on the how the other systems are working (fuel, ignition etc) and how hard your are driving it.  A quick easy way to see if you have an exhaust restriction is to slap a vacuum gauge on it.  The backflow causes less air to be sucked and hence less vacuum.  <BR>Also, the cat could be clean as a whistle but the blown out contents may then plug the muffler.  Same effect from both.   GL||||reg||1
Z||000023||sqoach||10-31-2001||12:26 PM||||My SE use to run kinda crappy like yours is. Then I took out the converter and it runs much better and has more power on the low end and the high end. I don't recall the manifolds glowing. I'm sure I would have noticed if they were. When I took it out, it was crap. Bunch of black stuff just fell out.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
